# Kept deliberately, even though it is empty.
#
# apps/web/Dockerfile copies `/repo/apps/web/public` into the runtime image
# unconditionally, and Docker fails a COPY whose source does not exist. Next.js
# does not require a public directory, so nothing else would have created one —
# the image build simply fails on a fresh clone with an error that reads as a
# Dockerfile bug rather than a missing directory.
#
# Delete this only together with that COPY line.
